{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>Take Me a heifer of three years old.</b> Concerning this vision the opinions are many; I too will answer my portion and say: Since we find in the promise of the land that He sometimes mentions the fathers and sometimes their seed — but where do we find that the fathers had a portion in the land? Were they not all sojourners in the land? And the verse says ״כִּי לְךָ אֶתְּנֶנָּה״ (Genesis 15:7), and it is written (Exodus 6:8) ״לָתֵת אוֹתָהּ לְאַבְרָהָם לְיִצְחָק וּלְיַעֲקֹב״ etc. Therefore our Rabbis of blessed memory learned (Sanhedrin 90b) from here a proof for the resurrection of the dead from the Torah, for it says (Exodus 6:4) ״לָתֵת לָהֶם״ — ״לָכֶם״ is not said, but rather ״לָהֶם״. But this too lacks explanation: would the fathers inherit a portion in the land in this world because of the resurrection of the dead?" "Rather, this is nothing but burial — that they would receive their portion to have a burial place in the land, for all who die in the land of Israel are first to live at the time to come, as will be explained with the help of HaShem in the portion of Va'era (Exodus 6:3). But their seed received their portion also while alive in this world, and the fathers specifically after death, when they shall live first. Therefore the Holy One, blessed be He, showed him in this vision: a heifer corresponding to Abram, concerning whom it is said of him (Genesis 18:7) ״וְאֶל הַבָּקָר רָץ אַבְרָהָם״. And a goat corresponding to Jacob, who clothed his neck with the skins of goat-kids. And a ram corresponding to Isaac, who offered his substitute, a ram. And so Rashi explained in the portion of Naso regarding the offerings of the princes (Numbers 7:21). And a turtledove and a young pigeon — these are Israel. ״וַיְבַתֵּר אֹתָם בַּתָּוֶךְ״ — He hinted that these three fathers specifically after cutting, that is, after death, would receive their portion in the land, for the dead of the land of Israel live first, but not while alive. ״וְאֶת הַצִּפֹּר לֹא בָתָר״ — for Israel, who are likened to a turtledove and a young pigeon, will come to the land alive, for in this the Holy One, blessed be He, showed him who and who are those going to the land, and in what manner the fathers would have a portion in the land — and that is after cutting and death, that is, after their sun sets in this world, when the slumber of death falls upon them. This is what is said ״וַיְהִי הַשֶּׁמֶשׁ לָבוֹא וְתַרְדֵּמָה נָפְלָה עַל אַבְרָם״, as it is stated (Ecclesiastes 12:2) ״עַד אֲשֶׁר לֹא תֶחְשַׁךְ הַשֶּׁמֶשׁ״, to teach: when Abram lies down and sleeps, then he will receive his portion in the land — but not now, for ״לֹא שָׁלֵם עֲוֹן הָאֱמֹרִי עַד הֵנָּה״. And the children of Israel will be those who come to the land after the setting of Abram's sun and the slumber of death, as stated." "But on this condition — ״כִּי גֵר יִהְיֶה זַרְעֲךָ בְּאֶרֶץ לֹא לָהֶם״ — not theirs at first, ״וַעֲבָדוּם״. And the fact that He began in singular language ״זַרְעֲךָ״, and afterward said ״וַעֲבָדוּם״ in plural language — is because the sojourning began from the birth of Isaac, and the fathers were individuals, but the servitude began after they multiplied. And what is said ״בְּאֶרֶץ לֹא לָהֶם״, some say it refers to the people of the land, for they too are sojourners in their own land, as they learned from the verse (Genesis 47:21) ״וְאֶת הָעָם הֶעֱבִיר אֹתוֹ לֶעָרִים״, so that they would not call Israel exiles. And the fact that He mentioned four things — sojourning, and servitude, and affliction, and the distance of the Shekhinah in a land not theirs — will be explained with the help of HaShem further on in the portion of Va'era (Exodus 6:6). And the reason for the number four hundred will be explained with the help of HaShem in the portion of Chayei Sarah (Genesis 23:16)."], :book :genesis, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}],